[section:WriteMultiToken Multiple-datagram write token requirements]

A multiple-datagram write token is a
[link asio.overview.model.completion_tokens completion token] for completion
signature `void(error_code, size_t)`, where the second argument is the number
of datagrams sent.

[heading Examples]

A free function as a multiple-datagram write token:

  void send_handler(
      const asio::error_code& ec,
      std::size_t messages_transferred)
  {
    ...
  }

A multiple-datagram write token function object:

  struct send_handler
  {
    ...
    void operator()(
        const asio::error_code& ec,
        std::size_t messages_transferred)
    {
      ...
    }
    ...
  };

A lambda as a multiple-datagram write token:

  socket.async_send_multiple(...,
      [](const asio::error_code& ec,
        std::size_t messages_transferred)
      {
        ...
      });

A non-static class member function adapted to a multiple-datagram write token
using `std::bind()`:

  void my_class::send_handler(
      const asio::error_code& ec,
      std::size_t messages_transferred)
  {
    ...
  }
  ...
  socket.async_send_multiple(...,
      std::bind(&my_class::send_handler,
        this, std::placeholders::_1,
        std::placeholders::_2));

A non-static class member function adapted to a multiple-datagram write token
using `boost::bind()`:

  void my_class::send_handler(
      const asio::error_code& ec,
      std::size_t messages_transferred)
  {
    ...
  }
  ...
  socket.async_send_multiple(...,
      boost::bind(&my_class::send_handler,
        this, asio::placeholders::error,
        asio::placeholders::messages_transferred));

Using [link asio.reference.use_future use_future] as a multiple-datagram write
token:

  std::future<std::size_t> f =
    socket.async_send_multiple(..., asio::use_future);
  ...
  try
  {
    std::size_t n = f.get();
    ...
  }
  catch (const system_error& e)
  {
    ...
  }

Using [link asio.reference.use_awaitable use_awaitable] as a multiple-datagram
write token:

  asio::awaitable<void> my_coroutine()
  {
    try
    {
      ...
      std::size_t n =
        co_await socket.async_send_multiple(
            ..., asio::use_awaitable);
      ...
    }
    catch (const system_error& e)
    {
      ...
    }
  }

[endsect]
